    {
      "id": "f2862736-35fa-4b53-879f-51a2c27969ec",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 896,
        "content": "## Tenant Churn Prediction & Retention Automation\n\n### How it works\n\nThis workflow runs a daily tenant churn scan, reads tenant master data from Google Sheets, and processes each tenant in a loop. It computes churn signals such as payment friction, maintenance friction, lease proximity, and AI-derived sentiment, then calculates a weighted risk score and assigns a risk tier. Based on the tier, it updates the CRM sheet and sends the appropriate Slack or Gmail retention action, with separate Slack notifications for scan completion and workflow failures.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Connect Google Sheets credentials and configure the tenant master/CRM sheets used for reading tenant data and writing risk flags.\n- Configure the CONFIG node with the desired weighting values for payment, maintenance, and sentiment risk factors.\n- Connect Google Gemini credentials for the sentiment analysis agent and confirm the selected Gemini model is available.\n- Connect Slack credentials and set the channels or recipients for high-risk alerts, scan completion notices, and workflow failure notifications.\n- Connect Gmail credentials and verify the sender account, recipient fields, and email templates for medium- and low-risk tenant outreach.\n- Enable and adjust the daily schedule trigger to run at the desired churn scan time.\n\n### Customization\n\nAdjust the risk-weighting formula, tier thresholds, Slack alert copy, email subjects/bodies, and the Google Sheets columns to match the property management team’s retention process."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "49247221-774a-4b9f-a848-d8e8f71de4a8",
